  created)
DESCRIPTION:Mechanisms in Motion\, Episode 01. 105-min block: 15 setup + 
 75 record + 15 buffer. The guest's local track is the one irreplaceable 
 asset\; protect it (upload marshal + archive below).\n\nDO\n- T-minus 5 
 min\, BEFORE the guest joins: both hosts confirm the MV7+ is chosen as t
 he microphone in Riverside's settings (a software pick\, not just pluggi
 ng it in)\, 'separate tracks / local recording' is ON (in Riverside's St
 udio settings\; it saves each person's audio to their own computer as in
 surance)\, and the QuickTime backup is rolling. Fix any before admitting
  the guest.\n- Headphones on for everyone (kills echo).\n- Hit Record\; 
 say the slate ('Episode N\, take 1')\; pause 3 seconds silent for sync.\
 n- Record ~60 min of conversation. If a guest's audio is rough\, ask the
 m live to move closer\, turn off fans/AC\, and put on headphones.\n- UPL
 OAD MARSHAL: one host's only end-of-session job is to watch EVERY track 
 (including the GUEST's) to 100% in the Riverside dashboard. The other ho
 st handles the goodbye. The guest is NOT released until the marshal call
 s 'clear.'\n- If a track is missing or stalls\, do NOT end the call: kee
 p the guest on while it re-uploads\; if it can't\, rebook on the spot wh
 ile you have them.\n- Archive immediately: both QuickTime backups + the 
 Riverside download go to the shared cloud folder 'MiM-EpNN-Guest-YYYY-MM
 -DD/' before any editing.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Clean separate local tr
 acks captured\; slate + 3-sec sync pause\; GUEST track confirmed 100% be
